## Configuring the router

1. Click Branch-R1: select CLI and press enter
(The router will become the default gateway for each subnet!)
2. Enter privilege mode: 
      type enable

3. Then enter global configuration mode: 
      type configure terminal or config t

4. Give the router a hostname if you like
      type hostname Branch-R1
(The prompt will change to now Branch-R1(config)#:

5. Configure the Guest interface
  interface gigabitEthernet 0/0               <- selecting the interface
  ip address 192.168.10.1 255.255.255.128     <-  giving it the Guest gateway address
  no shutdown                                 <- turning the interface on
  exit
                                              (the router interface is gigabitEthernet 0/0)
Guest now has: Gateway 192.168.10.1
               Mask: 255.255.255.128

6. Configure the Sales interface
 interface gigabitEthernet 0/1
 ip address 192.168.10.129 255.255.255.192
 no shutdown
 exit

Sales now has: Gateway 192.168.10.129
               Mask: 255.255.255.192

7. Configure the Engineering interface
interface gigabitEthernet 0/2
ip address 192.168.19.193 255.255.255.224
no shutdown
exit

Engineering now has: Gateway 192.168.10.193
                     Mask: 255.255.255.224

8. Verify the router 
You can run: show ip interface brief
You would see something similar to:

Interface           IP-Address      Status  Protocol
GigabetEthernet0/0  192.168.10.1    up        up
GigabitEthernet0/1  192.168.10.129  up        up
GigabitEthernet0/2  192.168.10.193  up        up

9. Save the configuration:
  copy running-config startup-config
(when prompted for the destination filename, press ENTER twice)

10. Configure SW-Guest
Click on SW-Guest then select CLI.
Press the enter key:
    enable
    config t
    hostname SW-Guest

Now give the switch a management IP:
    interface vlan 1
    ip address 192.168.10.3 255.255.255.128
    no shutdown
    exit

Set the default gateway:
    ip default-gateway 192.168.10.1

Then save your configuration!
    end
    copy running-config startup-config

